The fix saves the allocated auxiliary device ID in a local variable `id` before attempting `auxiliary_device_add()`. After a failure and the call to `auxiliary_device_uninit()`, the cleanup path uses the local `id` instead of the freed `adev->id`, eliminating the use-after-free. The saved integer value remains valid regardless of the memory release.

